Certainly! To embed AcmeBank's contact widget on your intranet page, you'll need to use an HTML snippet that includes the necessary script tags to load the widget. Here’s a basic example of how you can do this:

```html
<div id="acmebank-contact-widget"></div>
<script src="https://widget.acmebank.com/widget.js"></script>
<script>
  (function() {
    var widget = document.createElement('script');
    widget.type = 'text/javascript';
    widget.async = true;
    widget.src = 'https://widget.acmebank.com/widget.js';
    widget.id = 'acmebank-contact-widget';
    var s = document.getElementsByTagName('script')[0];
    s.parentNode.insertBefore(widget, s);
  })();
</script>
```

This snippet creates a placeholder `<div>` where the widget will be inserted and includes the script to load the widget from our server. Make sure to customize the `id` attribute if you need multiple instances of the widget on the same page.

